Yes. Under Clause 2.2 of the NDA, the Receiving Party may disclose Confidential Information to its “Representatives,” which are defined to include employees, but only if the employees need to know the Confidential Information for the Purpose.

This disclosure is subject to conditions, including that the Receiving Party must:

1. inform the Representatives of the confidential nature of the information before disclosure;  
2. ensure the Representatives comply with the Agreement as if they were the Receiving Party, and if requested, procure that a relevant Representative enters into a confidentiality agreement with the Disclosing Party on equivalent terms;  
3. keep a written record of the Representatives to whom information was disclosed; and  
4. remain liable for any failure by the Representatives to comply with the Agreement.
